<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Helü of Wu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 514–496 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as He Lü</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helü was king of Wu from 514 to 496 BCE, after seizing the throne by having his cousin King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> assassinated. Advised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zixu">Wu Zixu</a> and, by tradition, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-tzu">Sun Tzu</a>, he defeated Chu at Boju and took its capital Ying in 506 BCE, making Wu a great power. He died of a wound received fighting the State of Yue at Zuili in 496 BCE.</p></div>
